Technical Details
Frontend Technology Stack
Core Framework

React.js (v18+): Used for building the user interface with functional components and hooks.

React provides a component-based architecture that makes it easy to build and maintain complex user interfaces.
Functional components with hooks are used throughout the application for better code organization and reusability.



State Management

Zustand: A lightweight state management solution preferred over Redux for simplicity.

Zustand provides a simple API for managing global application state without the boilerplate of Redux.
Custom stores are created for different aspects of the application (editor state, project data, user settings).



2D Editor Technology

Konva.js with react-konva: Provides the canvas-based drawing capabilities.

The canvas is organized into multiple layers for better performance and organization:

Background layer for grid and room outline
Wall layer for room structure
Object layer for furniture and fixtures
Annotation layer for dimensions and labels


Custom event handling is implemented to manage selection, transformation, and tool interactions.
Performance optimizations include layer caching and selective rerendering.



3D Visualization

Three.js with react-three-fiber: Enables 3D rendering and visualization.

react-three-fiber provides a React-friendly way to work with Three.js.
@react-three/drei is used for common Three.js helpers and controls.
Custom hooks manage the synchronization between 2D and 3D representations.
Optimizations include:

Level of Detail (LOD) for complex models
Instancing for duplicate objects
Frustum culling to only render visible objects
Texture compression and delayed loading





Routing and Navigation

React Router (v6): Handles application routing and navigation.

Browser router is used for clean URLs.
Protected routes ensure authenticated access to certain pages.
Route-based code splitting is implemented for performance.



UI Component Library

Custom UI Components with Tailwind CSS: For consistent styling and responsive design.

Tailwind provides utility classes for rapid UI development.
Custom component library extends Tailwind for application-specific components.
Design tokens ensure consistent colors, spacing, and typography.



API Communication

Axios: Handles HTTP requests to the backend.

Request interceptors add authentication headers.
Response interceptors handle common errors.
Cancelable requests prevent race conditions.



Drag and Drop Functionality

Custom Drag and Drop System: Built on native browser APIs for performance.

Integrates with Konva for canvas interactions.
Supports dragging items from library to canvas.
Implements preview and snapping behavior.



File Handling and Export

PDF Generation: Using jsPDF for creating exportable plans.
Image Export: Canvas/WebGL to Blob conversion for high-resolution exports.
Data Export: JSON serialization with structured formatting.

Backend Technology Stack
Server Framework

Node.js with Express.js: Provides the API server functionality.

RESTful API design with versioned endpoints.
Middleware architecture for request processing.
Rate limiting and security headers for protection.



Database

MongoDB with Mongoose: Document database for flexible data storage.

Schemas enforce data structure while allowing flexibility for project data.
Indexing is applied to frequently queried fields.
Aggregation pipeline used for complex data transformations.



Authentication

Passport.js with JWT: Handles user authentication and authorization.

JSON Web Tokens (JWT) for stateless authentication.
Multiple strategies support (local, Google, Apple).
Token refresh mechanism for extended sessions.
bcrypt for secure password hashing.



AI Integration

OpenAI API Integration: Powers the chat and design assistance.

System prompts establish design assistant capabilities.
Context management to maintain conversation history.
Structured output formatting for JSON parsing.
Rate limiting and error handling for API stability.



Estimation Engine

Custom Estimation Algorithms: Calculate costs based on materials, labor, and features.

Rule-based pricing for standard items.
Area-based calculations for materials.
Regional adjustment factors for pricing accuracy.
Material quantity algorithms account for waste and packaging.



Development and Deployment Infrastructure
Development Tools

ESLint and Prettier: Code quality and formatting.
Jest and React Testing Library: Unit and integration testing.
Husky: Pre-commit hooks for code quality.

CI/CD Pipeline

GitHub Actions: Automated testing and deployment.

Separate workflows for testing and deployment.
Environment-specific deployment configurations.
Automated versioning and release notes.



Deployment Targets

Frontend: Vercel or Netlify for static site hosting.

CDN integration for fast content delivery.
Edge functions for API proxying.
Automatic preview deployments for pull requests.


Backend: AWS Elastic Beanstalk or similar managed service.

Auto-scaling configuration for handling load.
Database connection pooling for efficiency.
Load balancing for high availability.



Monitoring and Analytics

Sentry.io: Error tracking and performance monitoring.

Real-time error alerts.
Performance tracing for slow operations.
User impact analysis for prioritizing fixes.


Custom Analytics: User behavior tracking for product improvement.

Feature usage metrics.
User flow analysis.
Conversion tracking for key actions.



Performance Optimizations
Frontend Performance

Code Splitting: Lazy loading of components for faster initial load.
Asset Optimization: Compression and CDN for static assets.
Virtualization: For large lists and object libraries to reduce DOM size.
Memoization: Strategic use of React.memo and useMemo to prevent unnecessary rerenders.
WebWorkers: For CPU-intensive operations to keep UI responsive.

3D Rendering Performance

Adaptive Quality: Automatic quality adjustments based on device capability.
Geometry Optimization: Simplified meshes for distant objects.
Shader Optimization: Custom shaders for specific effects over general-purpose ones.
Texture Atlasing: Combined textures to reduce draw calls.